/target/
/r-build/target/
/r-build/vendor/
/src/rust/r-build/target/
/src/CellChat.so
/.rlib/
*.log

# R's default graphics device output. Any Rscript that draws without an explicit device leaves one
# behind, and it is a build artifact, not source.
/Rplots.pdf
# `R CMD build` output. Rebuilt by the release script; never committed.
/cellchatrs_*.tar.gz
/cellchatrs.Rcheck/
# A leftover dump of the MT19937 reference run. The fixture itself is
# tests/fixtures/rng_golden.txt, which is what the tests read; this file was a stray
# redirect of the same output and had no reader.
/stdout

# A runner that refuses to measure writes this beside its output. It is evidence of *why* a
# measurement was declined, not a result, so it never belongs in the repository.
bench-runner/results/*.refused.json

/CellChat_*.tar.gz
/CellChat.Rcheck/

# Real single-cell datasets: 70 MB of .rda/.rds. They are benchmark *inputs*, not package
# content -- nothing under R/, tests/ or vignettes/ reads them, `.Rbuildignore` already keeps
# them out of the source tarball, and `scripts/fetch_ci_fixtures.sh` fetches each one by a
# pinned file id and asserts its exact byte size and sha256. That script is the reason they are
# not in the repository: committing 70 MB of binaries that nothing in the package needs, and
# that git would then have to store forever, buys nothing the fetch does not already give.
# The benchmark runners find them via `CELLCHATRS_DATA`, defaulting to `data/`.
/data/humanSkin.rda
/data/wound.rda
/data/visium.rds
